      "id": "at-glance",
      "title": "At a glance",
      "body": "For travelers, Tôi không hiểu is the phrase to keep ready for \"I don't understand\" in moments when Vietnamese stops making sense. This is for when someone is speaking too quickly or using unfamiliar words. Lead with this before you ask for a repeat or a simpler version. It works best when you focus on asking for one clear help action before adding more words. After you say it, listen for a slower repeat, a pointed explanation, or a switch to writing; the next rows help you keep the exchange moving.",
      "presentation": "plain-text"
    },
    {
